cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "VISTA v2: strategy-proof receiver decisions over attested evidence for agentic and real-time payments"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sarang109/vista_2"
authors:
  - family-names: Kulkarni
    given-names: Sarang Shrikant
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Austin, Texas, United States
abstract: >-
  Research artifact for the paper "Strategy-Proof Fraud Decisions over Attested Evidence for Real-Time and
  Agentic Payments". It implements control-typed evidence games, the reachability characterization of
  strategy-proof receiver decision rules, the evaluation-gap and splitting experiments, conservative monotone
  repair, an issuer-signed cumulative-spend claim, and the agentic and disclosure-privacy experiments, with
  the full five-seed results.
keywords:
  - payment fraud
  - strategy-proof decisions
  - attested evidence
  - agentic payments
  - strategic classification
  - selective disclosure
